                    ## Task goal                                                
                                                                                
                    I am a dermatologist, I have collected                      
                    data about skin lesions with my                             
                    colleagues over the last years. Now I                       
                    want to train an AI on this dataset                         
                    that can differentiate malignant and                        
                    benign lesions. The idea is that I                          
                    upload a folder with new images and the                     
                    model returns the probability between 0                     
                    and 1 for each image that the image                         
                    shows a malignant skin lesion.                              
                                                                                
                    ## Task evaluation                                          
                                                                                
                    Area under the receiver operator curve                      
                    (AUROC)                                                     
                                                                                
                    # Memory                                                    
                                                                                
                    Design: We fine-tune a pretrained                           
                    ResNet18 on the skin lesion images,                         
                    mapping malignant to 1 and                                  
                    benign/non-neoplastic to 0. We split                        
                    the data into train and validation                          
                    sets, apply standard image                                  
                    augmentations for training and                              
                    normalization for both, and train with                      
                    Adam and BCEWithLogitsLoss for a few                        
                    epochs. After training, we compute and                      
                    print the AUROC on the hold-out                             
                    validation set. We also provide a                           
                    reusable predict() function that takes                      
                    a folder of images and returns                              
                    malignancy probabilities.                                   
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model was trained for 3 epochs on the                       
                    skin lesion dataset and achieved a                          
                    validation AUROC of 0.8852, indicating                      
                    good discrimination between malignant                       
                    and benign lesions. The training loss                       
                    decreased steadily across epochs,                           
                    showing effective learning.                                 
                    Validation Metric: 0.8852                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose integrating a                             
                    OneCycle learning rate scheduler to                         
                    improve convergence and generalization.                     
                    We will set a higher maximum learning                       
                    rate (e.g., 1e-3) and schedule it over                      
                    all training iterations, stepping the                       
                    scheduler after each batch. This often                      
                    leads to better performance than a                          
                    fixed or decaying learning rate. The                        
                    rest of the training pipeline remains                       
                    unchanged.                                                  
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model trained for 3 epochs with                             
                    decreasing loss values, indicating                          
                    effective learning. The validation                          
                    AUROC achieved was 0.8477, which                            
                    demonstrates good model performance in                      
                    distinguishing malignant from benign                        
                    skin lesions.                                               
                    Validation Metric: 0.8477                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I will use PyTorch’s                                
                    mixed‐precision training                                    
                    (torch.cuda.amp) to speed up                                
                    forward/backward passes, increase                           
                    DataLoader workers, and reduce the                          
                    number of epochs to ensure the run                          
                    finishes within the time limit. A                           
                    GradScaler manages loss scaling, and we                     
                    keep the ROC AUC evaluation on the                          
                    hold‐out set unchanged. This will                           
                    greatly cut training time while                             
                    maintaining accuracy.                                       
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model trained for 3 epochs with                             
                    decreasing training loss, indicating                        
                    learning progress. The validation AUROC                     
                    reached 0.8665, which suggests good                         
                    model performance in distinguishing                         
                    malignant from benign skin lesions.                         
                    Validation Metric: 0.8665                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose integrating MixUp                         
                    data augmentation during training to                        
                    improve regularization and                                  
                    generalization. MixUp combines pairs of                     
                    images and their labels using a mixing                      
                    coefficient sampled from a Beta                             
                    distribution. This is an atomic change                      
                    in the training loop and can boost                          
                    AUROC without altering the model                            
                    architecture or overall pipeline.                           
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without errors. The                            
                    training loss decreased over the 3                          
                    epochs, indicating effective learning.                      
                    The validation AUROC of 0.8757                              
                    demonstrates good model performance in                      
                    distinguishing malignant from benign                        
                    skin lesions.                                               
                    Validation Metric: 0.8757                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: We can greatly speed up                             
                    training by freezing the DenseNet                           
                    backbone and precomputing image                             
                    features only once, then fitting a                          
                    lightweight sklearn logistic regression                     
                    in a 5‐fold stratified CV loop.  We                         
                    extract features via a small PyTorch                        
                    “FeatureExtractor” model using the                          
                    pretrained DenseNet121, store these as                      
                    NumPy arrays, and then train/predict                        
                    with logistic regression, which is                          
                    orders of magnitude faster.  For                            
                    inference we extract test‐set features                      
                    similarly and average the per‐fold                          
                    logistic‐regression probabilities to                        
                    produce our submission.csv.                                 
                    Results: The code executed successfully                     
                    without any errors. The feature                             
                    extraction using DenseNet121 and                            
                    subsequent 5-fold cross-validation with                     
                    logistic regression produced consistent                     
                    AUROC scores around 0.86, indicating                        
                    good model performance in                                   
                    differentiating malignant from benign                       
                    skin lesions. The processing time was                       
                    reasonable given the dataset size.                          
                    Validation Metric: 0.8615                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose replacing the                             
                    ResNet18 backbone with a more powerful                      
                    EfficientNet‐B0 model pretrained on                         
                    ImageNet, which often yields better                         
                    feature representations and higher                          
                    accuracy for image classification                           
                    tasks. We will swap out the model                           
                    instantiation to use                                        
                    `torchvision.models.efficientnet_b0`,                       
                    adjust its final classifier to output a                     
                    single logit, and keep all other                            
                    pipeline components (data loading,                          
                    transforms, training loop, and                              
                    evaluation) unchanged. This swap is an                      
                    atomic change that should boost the                         
                    AUROC without altering the training                         
                    procedure.                                                  
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model was trained for 3 epochs using an                     
                    EfficientNet-B0 backbone and achieved a                     
                    strong validation AUROC of 0.9082,                          
                    indicating good performance in                              
                    differentiating malignant from benign                       
                    skin lesions. The training loss                             
                    decreased steadily over epochs, showing                     
                    effective learning.                                         
                    Validation Metric: 0.9082                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose to implement                              
                    test‐time augmentation by averaging                         
                    predictions over the original and                           
                    horizontally flipped versions of each                       
                    image. During validation and in the                         
                    `predict()` function, we will compute                       
                    logits for both the image and its flip,                     
                    average the logits before applying the                      
                    sigmoid, and thereby obtain more robust                     
                    probability estimates. This TTA                             
                    approach can boost AUROC without any                        
                    additional training overhead. All other                     
                    parts of the pipeline remain unchanged.                     
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    training loss decreased steadily over 3                     
                    epochs, indicating effective learning.                      
                    The validation AUROC with test-time                         
                    augmentation (TTA) reached 0.9121,                          
                    demonstrating good model performance in                     
                    distinguishing malignant from benign                        
                    skin lesions.                                               
                    Validation Metric: 0.9121                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: We can address the timeout by                       
                    reducing the image resolution to                            
                    128×128 and freezing the pretrained                         
                    backbone so that only the final                             
                    classification layer is trained. This                       
                    greatly cuts down on per‐batch                              
                    computation while preserving                                
                    transfer‐learning performance. We                           
                    update the data transforms accordingly,                     
                    disable gradients for all backbone                          
                    parameters, and only optimize the final                     
                    `fc` layer. The rest of the pipeline,                       
                    including mixup, AUROC evaluation, and                      
                    the `predict` function that writes                          
                    `submission.csv`, remains intact.                           
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model was trained for 3 epochs using a                      
                    pretrained ResNet18 with frozen                             
                    backbone layers and mixup data                              
                    augmentation. The validation AUROC                          
                    achieved was 0.7699, indicating a                           
                    reasonably good performance in                              
                    distinguishing malignant from benign                        
                    skin lesions. Predictions were                              
                    successfully saved to a CSV file.                           
                    Validation Metric: 0.7699                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: We will switch to a single                          
                    stratified train/validation split and                       
                    lower the image size to 160×160 to cut                      
                    compute, freeze the MobileNetV3                             
                    backbone so only the classifier head is                     
                    trained, and train for just three                           
                    epochs. After training we compute and                       
                    print the hold‐out AUROC, save the best                     
                    model, and then use a reusable                              
                    predict() function to score all images                      
                    in the input folder and write a                             
                    submission.csv file with image_name and                     
                    probability. The predict() function is                      
                    fully documented and can be called on                       
                    new image folders with a list of model                      
                    checkpoints.                                                
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model was trained for 3 epochs with a                       
                    MobileNetV3 small backbone, achieving a                     
                    best validation AUROC of 0.8195. The                        
                    script also generated predictions for                       
                    all images and saved a submission file                      
                    with 16,577 entries, indicating proper                      
                    end-to-end functionality.                                   
                    Validation Metric: 0.8195                                   
                                                                                
